      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A thought: wouldn't that make it hard to tell if a tracker is inside your geometry or not? You wouldn't be able to perceive depth.\n\nI find that using the spiky models are useful for this case -- even if a tracker is inside my leg or hip, I can still suss out where it is thanks to it being stuck inside the mesh and knowing the spikes stick out from the center.\n\n(If you didn't know, you can change what model the trackers are using in the big settings menu under IK & Tracking!)",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
